d3d12: Do not release suballocated BOs while creating a BO

d3d12_bo_new releases the BOs whose last use the GPU has completed, before
and while retrying CreateCommittedResource. A pipebuffer slab manager
creates its slabs with its lock held (pb_slab_manager_create_buffer, then
pb_slab_create), through the cache manager to d3d12_bo_new, and releasing
a suballocated BO, one of that manager's buffers, takes the same lock
(pb_slab_buffer_destroy): the thread waited on itself. Under gfxstream's
OpenGL ES translator, a glBufferData hung that way, and with it every
display of the Android guest.

d3d12_bo_new now keeps suballocated BOs queued, at the head of the list,
for the next reclaim, which batch completion and resource destruction run
without that lock; it waits only for BOs it may release.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_bufmgr.cpp	2026-10-30 16:54:42.802209577 -0300
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_bufmgr.cpp	2026-10-30 16:55:00.882635382 -0300
@@ -113,6 +113,11 @@
    return bo;
 }
 
+static bool
+reclaim_completed(struct d3d12_screen *screen, bool keep_suballocated);
+static bool
+reclaim_one(struct d3d12_screen *screen, bool keep_suballocated);
+
